# Embed Annotations & Highlights Directly Into the PDF

## Problem

Currently, all annotations (pen strokes, text highlights, text notes) live exclusively in the ViewModel's in-memory state (`PdfReaderState.strokesByPage`, `highlightsByPage`, `textAnnotationsByPage`). They are rendered as Compose Canvas overlays on top of the PDF bitmap. This means:

1. **Annotations are lost** when the user closes the document or the app is killed.
2. **Annotations leak across documents** — the state maps are keyed by page index and are never cleared on `OpenPdf`, so opening a second PDF will show annotations from the first.
3. **The physical PDF file is never modified** — other PDF readers (Adobe, Google Drive viewer, etc.) will never see these annotations.

## Proposed Approach

Use **Apache PDFBox** (already a dependency at `2.0.27.0`) to write standard PDF annotation objects into the file structure before syncing it back via SAF. PDFBox supports:

| Annotation Type | PDFBox Class | PDF Spec Type |
|---|---|---|
| Text Highlights | `PDAnnotationTextMarkup` | `/Highlight` |
| Pen (Freehand Ink) | `PDAnnotationRubberStamp` → actually `PDAnnotationMarkup` subclass — we'll use the ink approach via COS dictionary | `/Ink` |
| Text Notes | `PDAnnotationText` | `/Text` (sticky note) |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Coordinate System Flip**: The app stores all annotation coordinates as **normalized 0→1 values measured from the top-left**. PDF spec uses points measured from the **bottom-left**. Every coordinate must be converted: `pdfY = pageHeight - (normalizedY × pageHeight)`.

---

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> **Overwrite Behavior**: When saving, the annotated PDF will be written back to the **same source URI** via SAF. This permanently modifies the original file (including Google Drive copies). If you want a "Save Copy" option instead, let me know and I'll add a separate flow.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No Undo After Save**: Once annotations are baked into the PDF and synced back, they become part of the file. The eraser tool will still work on in-memory annotations before the next save, but previously saved annotations become permanent PDF objects. Do you want a "flatten on close" or an explicit "Save Annotations" button in the toolbar?

