## Proposed Changes

### Data Layer — New `PdfAnnotationWriter`

#### [NEW] [PdfAnnotationWriter.kt](file:///x:/AI_and_Automation/pdf-reader/app/src/main/java/com/pdfreader/app/data/pdfbox/PdfAnnotationWriter.kt)

A new class in `data/pdfbox/` responsible for writing annotations into a `PDDocument`:

- **`writeHighlights(document, pageIndex, highlights, pageSize)`** — Converts each `TextHighlight.rects` (normalized 0–1, top-left origin) into `PDAnnotationTextMarkup` objects with proper `QuadPoints` and `Rectangle` in PDF coordinate space (bottom-left origin, measured in points).
- **`writeInkStrokes(document, pageIndex, strokes, pageSize)`** — Converts each `FreehandStroke.points` into a `PDAnnotationInk` with `inkList` (list of `float[]` paths) and a computed bounding `PDRectangle`.
- **`writeTextAnnotations(document, pageIndex, annotations, pageSize)`** — Converts each `TextAnnotation` into a `PDAnnotationText` (sticky note icon) at the correct position.
- **`writeAllAnnotations(document, state)`** — Convenience method that iterates all pages and delegates to the above.

Key implementation detail — coordinate conversion:
```kotlin
// Normalized (0..1, top-left origin) → PDF points (bottom-left origin)
fun normalizedToPdf(nx: Float, ny: Float, pageWidth: Float, pageHeight: Float): Pair<Float, Float> {
    return Pair(nx * pageWidth, pageHeight - (ny * pageHeight))
}
```

